<title>USA: Celadon Group credit line extended.</title>
<headline>Celadon Group credit line extended.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Celadon Group Inc, a trucking company, on Tuesday said its banks extended the company's $30 million line of credit for two years.</p>
<p>The extension carries an interest rate of 162.5 basis points over the London Interbank Offer Rate, less than the previous rate of 200 basis points over LIBOR, the company said.</p>
<p>The rate can be lowered as the company's performance improves, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
